TEXT -80 8 Left 2 !.param tdv=1 tdt=1 fn1=50 omega_n={2*pi*fn1}\n.options vntol=1 abstol=100m reltol=0.001
TEXT -80 32 Left 2 !.tran 0 1 0 0.1m
TEXT -128 144 Left 2 ;ATP: R1=0.1626 X1=3,315 R0:1.502 X0:6.965
TEXT -128 -16 Left 2 ;Measurement of R1, R0, Rnn: coupled line with ATP-Matrix
TEXT -128 168 Left 2 ;see line_coupled.lib \nper km impedance matrix (only reactances used, resistance is above)\n+ XL11=4.576542E-01\n+ XM12=1.358979E-01 XL22=4.517972E-01\n+ XM13=9.094776E-02 XM23=1.358979E-01 XL33=4.576542E-01\nXM21=XM12 XM31=XM13 XM32=XM23
TEXT -128 240 Left 2 ;AT samephased operation: (all phases have 0 degrees therefore no 1,a,a^2 used which is for 120degrees difference)\nX0=(XL11+XM12+XM13)/3+(XL22+XM21+XM23)/3+(XL33+XM31+XM32)/3=6.970ohm (for 10km)\nR0=(R11+R12+R13)/3+(R22+R21+R23)/3+(R33+R31+R32)/3=1.5ohm (for 10km)\nZ0=sqrt(R0^2+X0^2)\n \nR1=(R11-0.5*R12-0.5*R13)/3+(R22-0.5*R21-0.5*R23)/3+(R33-0.5*R31-0.5*R32)/3=0.16ohm (for 10km)\nX1=(XL11-0.5*XM12-0.5*XM13)/3+(XL22-0.5*XM21-0.5*XM23)/3+(XL33-0.5*XM31-0.5*XM32)/3=3.3ohm (for 10km)\nZ1=sqrt(R1^2+X1^2)
TEXT 136 16 Left 2 ;If the uncoupled resistance from the ATP-Matrix is used R=U/I=1/6.15=0.162ohm which equals R1\nIn the coupled case with one voltage source the resistance=1/1.6341=0.612 which equals Rnn (R11,R22,R33)\nYou can use three voltage sources to obtain R0 = about 1.5ohm (for the coupled case)
TEXT 80 56 Left 2 ;Change the models with coupled and uncoupled R !!
TEXT 96 72 Left 2 ;per km resistive matrix for coupled r\nR11=0.06118 R12=0.04533 R13=0.04301 \nR22=0.061 R23=0.04533 \nR33=0.06118\nR21=R12 R31=R13 R32=R23
TEXT -144 104 Left 2 ;R0 measurement with R=U/I=1/0.6685\n=1.5ohm
TEXT 96 128 Left 2 ;NOTE: The coupled resistance models the resistivity of the return to earth path !!!
